WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.040
So we're waiting to see who will be in Joe
Biden's cabinet.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.620
And there have been a variety of different
names floated.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.360
Some have been denied, some have not been
denied.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.900
It's very interesting to look at the way that
all goes.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.770
And ultimately, we're going to know and we'll
do a deep dove about Joe Biden's cabinet.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:21.310
But as is often the case as a precursor to
selecting your cabinet, Joe Biden has selected

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.310
his chief of staff.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:27.350
This is his first major staff pick, of course,
the vice president, Kamala Harris, and a very

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.410
important selection which was made some time
ago.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.460
But for post-election, this is really good
news.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.380
Ronald Klain is going to be Joe Biden's chief
of staff.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.510
It's just a great choice.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:44.460
And everybody from Alexandria, Cassio Cortez
to centrist Democrats to Democratic consultants,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.920
everybody says this is a fantastic choice.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.980
And I'm going to tell you a little bit about
Ronald Klain.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.150
But when the bar is not not that Klain isn't
a good choice no matter what, but when the

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:02.870
bar is so low already because of Donald Trump,
Ronald Klain is an adult who is not only intelligent,

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.740
but he's organized and he gets things done.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.920
That's already going to be much better than
the people that Donald Trump has had as chiefs

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.020
of staff.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:17.889
Ronald Klain also happened to be Barack Obama's
Ebola czar during the Obama Biden administration.

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:24.179
And if we want to talk about signals when
Joe Biden selects Ronald Klain, it's a signal

00:01:24.179 --> 00:01:28.310
that he rejects the chaos of the Trump administration.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:34.749
He rejects the idea of these wild, loose cannon,
unhinged staffers in a lot of different positions.

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:36.009
I'm going to be very upfront.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:38.849
Ronald Klain is going to be a boring chief
of staff.

00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:41.700
He's going to be a sensible, sober chief of
staff.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:49.670
You're not likely to hear a lot from Ronald
Klain in terms of cartoonish incidents and

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.979
scandals and fiascos.

00:01:50.979 --> 00:01:55.270
And if you're dealing with a pandemic, as
Joe Biden is going to be, and unfortunately,

00:01:55.270 --> 00:02:02.289
because Donald Trump is just done with coronavirus,
a very serious pandemic on January 20th, Ronald

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:07.060
Klain is also particularly qualified because
he has experience dealing with medical outbreaks

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.170
already.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.180
He's a lawyer with a solid legal mind.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.940
He has a relatively progressive lean in terms
of what you would expect for a president like

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.090
Joe Biden.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:20.960
And he has the experience that is required
at exactly this time and again, widespread

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:21.960
praise.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:28.700
AOC tweeting, quote, Good news and an encouraging
choice, anti Trump Republicans, Steve Schmidt,

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.700
who's not our friend.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.890
But but the point is, everybody recognizes
Ronald Klain is a good choice.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:39.350
Steve Schmidt tweeting, Looks like the office
of chief of staff has just been upgraded by

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:46.120
one hundred gazillion percent with the appointment
of Ronald Klain squad member Congresswoman

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:51.230
Ayanna Pressley tweeting, quote, Having a
dedicated, humble, hardworking team around

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.880
you is everything.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:53.880
Congratulations.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:59.090
Ronald Klain encouraged to see you step into
this role and look forward to working together.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.810
Senator Elizabeth Warren tweeting, Ronald
Klain is a superb choice for chief of staff.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:08.060
He understands the magnitude of the health
and economic crisis and he has the experience

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.890
to lead this next administration through it.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.260
Ron has earned trust all across the entire
Democratic Party.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.670
I think you get it in Washington.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:22.090
You rarely see such unified and nearly unanimous
reaction to any choice for any position ever,

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.330
no matter how qualified the person is.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.650
He was on the ball.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:28.090
Ronald Klain was in terms of coronavirus.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:32.830
He wrote back in January, nearly 11 months
ago, a piece in the Atlantic where he said

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:37.180
or the piece was called Coronavirus is Coming
and Trump Isn't Ready.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.810
And he explained the ways in which Donald
Trump was not ready.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:47.520
So eventually we're going to be doing a deep
dove on Joe Biden's cabinet as it comes together,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.430
expecting some names around Thanksgiving time.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:57.260
But for now, the person who will be helping
Biden choose the cabinet is as close to.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:03.230
A perfect selection, as there could be, and
contrast it with Donald Trump's latest chief

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:09.670
of staff, Mark Meadows, who has been running
around Trump rallies with no mask high five

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.150
people, Mark Meadows caught coronavirus.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:18.349
Mark Meadows continue to insist that Donald
Trump would win, even though Donald Trump

00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:25.659
lost and said weeks ago, we are not going
to control the pandemic in what was arguably

00:04:25.659 --> 00:04:31.879
the most defeatist statement we've heard from
any administration official about the pandemic

00:04:31.879 --> 00:04:32.879
since the start.

00:04:32.879 --> 00:04:35.740
So change is very much in the air.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:40.550
I don't expect to agree with every cabinet
choice Joe Biden makes, but so far, this is

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.979
exactly what you would want to see.

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:43.740
Now, let me say one other thing.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.499
There have been I've been getting a lot of
emails from from people linking me to articles,

00:04:47.499 --> 00:04:52.729
some articles saying Warren and Bernie are
being considered for cabinet positions and

00:04:52.729 --> 00:04:58.469
other articles saying Warren and Bernie are
being frozen out of consideration for cabinet

00:04:58.469 --> 00:05:00.490
positions.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:04.639
With so many rumors floating around and so
many cabinet positions and so much else to

00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:12.080
talk about, I don't think there's much value
in me commenting on speculation about Biden's

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.639
cabinet.

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:16.569
When Biden chooses his cabinet, we will do
a deep dove.

00:05:16.569 --> 00:05:19.690
We will analyze every single cabinet member.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:20.939
Some of you will find it boring.

00:05:20.939 --> 00:05:22.139
Some of you will find it valuable.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:26.789
I think it's very important and we are going
to do that to sort of set up our understanding

00:05:26.789 --> 00:05:30.680
of the Biden administration as it comes in.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:37.930
One of the things I think is important to
think about is that when you select Democratic

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:42.069
senators to your cabinet, their Senate seats
open.

00:05:42.069 --> 00:05:47.280
Different states have different rules about
who and how gets to decide on their replacement.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:53.740
Here in Massachusetts, we have a Republican
governor currently and as at least as an interim

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.069
replacement to Elizabeth Warren until there's
a special election that may mean a Republican

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:01.699
senator replaces Elizabeth Warren in Vermont.

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:05.460
I actually don't know offhand exactly how
it goes.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:11.490
But while I obviously believe that Elizabeth
Warren and Bernie Sanders would be fantastic

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:15.419
cabinet selections, Bernie could be secretary
of Labor.

00:06:15.419 --> 00:06:17.180
There's other positions he could do.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:22.090
Elizabeth Warren could be secretary of education,
treasury secretary.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.879
You know, you could make an argument for either
of them as secretary of commerce.

00:06:25.879 --> 00:06:27.759
There's no doubt that these are qualified
people.

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:28.759
I do.

00:06:28.759 --> 00:06:30.819
And and I don't pretend to have an answer
to this question.

00:06:30.819 --> 00:06:31.900
It is it's not rhetorical.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.800
It's a real question.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.590
Are we better served by keeping Bernie and
Warren, the two most progressive members of

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.409
the Senate right now in the Senate?

00:06:42.409 --> 00:06:46.639
I think that that's a completely legitimate
question to be asking.

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:53.219
And given that you could pick people that
are arguably as good or almost as good as

00:06:53.219 --> 00:06:57.189
them for cabinet positions, although maybe
they would be less recognizable in terms of

00:06:57.189 --> 00:06:59.059
name recognition.

00:06:59.059 --> 00:07:01.520
Do we gain more by keeping them in the Senate?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:08.719
I think that almost certainly if Warren and
Bernie leave the Senate to be in Biden's cabinet,

00:07:08.719 --> 00:07:11.789
it's a guarantee that the Senate moves to
the right.

00:07:11.789 --> 00:07:15.960
When you take the two most liberal members
of the Senate and you replace them with people

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:21.370
that are arguably and almost certainly less
liberal, the average political orientation

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.290
of the Senate moves a little bit to the right.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:27.249
And I think that that's a perfectly legitimate
and important thing to be talking about.

00:07:27.249 --> 00:07:31.559
And we will discuss it if Democratic senators
do make it into Biden's cabinet.

00:07:31.559 --> 00:07:33.629
We will talk about it if they don't.

00:07:33.629 --> 00:07:35.589
And there are complaints, where is Bernie?

00:07:35.589 --> 00:07:36.669
Where is Warren?

00:07:36.669 --> 00:07:43.849
We will also talk about it completely fundamental
understanding of the reality of what happens

00:07:43.849 --> 00:07:46.879
when you take a Democratic senator out.

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:51.539
What happens to that seat of in the immediate
and also in the medium to long term when there

00:07:51.539 --> 00:07:53.059
is a special election?

00:07:53.059 --> 00:07:57.560
We'll have more about Ronald Klain and Biden's
cabinet on our Instagram page.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.009
Follow us there at David Pakman show.

00:08:00.009 --> 00:08:04.610
And listen, if you're already on Instagram,
follow me at David Pakman as well.

